    "spaceopera": {"title":"Star_Wars_(soundtrack)","kind":"work","why":"Los Angeles 1979 anchors the neo-romantic revival whose year zero is this record — March 1977, a symphony orchestra reading to picture when the idiom was believed dead — and the album article is the honest subject: the spyscore/polychoral one-work precedent, chosen over John Williams because the row is the revival and not the career, and over Film score, the craft survey goldenagescore's own row already refused."},
    "epichybrid": {"title":"Hans_Zimmer","kind":"artist","why":"Santa Monica 2010 is the braam's own year, and no genre article for the epic hybrid score exists in this ZIM (`Epic music` 404s; Film score is the refused craft survey) — so the row links the composer whose Santa Monica complex the idiom was literally built in, the goldenagescore/suspensescore artist precedent. The KEY stays a genre term per the round's naming law; the link names the man because the encyclopedia gave no other musical subject."},
    "trailerscore": {"title":"Trailer_music","kind":"broader","why":"Los Angeles 2012, and for once the genre article simply exists: 'Trailer music is the background music used for film previews' — the commission is the genre, the news pair's law, and the article says so in its first line. Not Two Steps from Hell, one library where this row is the trade."},
